// {"files":[{"path":"\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\danie\\OneDrive\\github-repos\\drosemann\\README.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":35,"oldLines":6,"newStart":35,"newLines":7,"lines":[" For storage I ended up with OneDrive 365 Basic with 100 GB for 2 euros a month, after years of being convinced I'd never give Microsoft a cent, until the Windows and Samsung integration won me over."," Speed doesn't matter much to me, and if OneDrive ever offers a 500 GB cold archive tier on very slow old hard drives for one or two euros a month, I'd be the first customer, and I'd probably store all my photos there too since 100 GB is easily enough for me."," I never actually needed it, since I never used more than two or three GB, but now I just upload 30 GB so I can say I use it.","+The stupid thing is I always said \"no SaaS subscriptions\", then October 2026 came and I ended up with two: OneDrive 100 GB and Muse Code for 4,29 €/mo. Back in April 2026 I predicted — and tagged Meta — that they should ship a $5/month tier with a lot of tokens: https://x.com/d5_iel/status/2113593415564771351 — and they actually did. Honest take though: I would have subscribed to whichever lab shipped a ~$5 tier first."," Long term I don't want just any job, I want to build my own thing and found an IT company for hosting, infrastructure and IT consulting, based on infra-pilot (https://github.com/drosemann/infra-pilot)."," I want scalable cloud solutions instead of generic root servers, built on pure Docker and KVM."," I also want to buy an old house, make it smart the cheap way, and document all of it on YouTube."]}]}]}
